Date: Sat, 2 Oct 1993 19:26:22 -0700 (PDT)
From: more@chaph.usc.edu (Max More)
Subject: Charging for being on the List.

The Extropy Institute Board is currently considering various options
regarding charging for staying on the Extropians e-mail list.  It does
cost ExI for each of the 300 or so people receiving the list.  We wish
to cover that -- plus a little more to help with the painfully tight
financial situation for ExI.  Many of you are not members of ExI, and
many do not even subscribe to EXTROPY.  We're considering making one
or both of these a requirement, though this seems unlikely to be the
option we'll choose.  Such a requirement may discourage too many people,
though it would have the advantage of ensuring that we have a common 
grounds for our discussions.  (Even this may not work, given the evidence
that some people don't even read the Welcome Message.)

To help with our decision, I'd appreciate your response to the following 
questions:

(1) How long have you been receiving the Extropians list?

(2) Would you discontinue your involvement if you were required to
pay a fee of $12/year?

(3) Would you discontinue your involvement if you were required, in
addition to the fee in (2), to subscribe to EXTROPY (@$18/year)?

(4) Would you discontinue your involvement if you were required to pay the fee,
and become a member of Extropy Institute ($30/year)?

Some sort of charge is practically inevitable (with a grace period of one-three
months for new list members), so that we can cover our costs and help ExI 
keep going.  Certainly 3c or 4c per day seems very little to ask for
the list to those who benefit from it.

Thanks Tim (May), and others who have raised these issues.  Apart from the
above options, we are considering others, such as (a) plus extra charges for
those wanting advanced software features.

Onward!

Max More		more@usc.edu
President		Extropy Institute (ExI)


