Deutsch devised the quantum computer primarily as a thought
experiment to make the Everett model testable, not as a
device for carrying out computations efficiently.

Now that a quantum computer is starting to approach the
realm of possibility people may well look at it
differently.

Objectivists that are knowledgeable about quantum mechanics
tend to believe in the Everett model, but it is not The
Revealed Truth by the Ghost of the Holy Rand. :-)

David Deutsch's thought experiment seemed convincing to me,
but then I already believed in the Everett model - collapse
of the wave functions seemed to me obviously absurd.

His thought experiment strains the collapse of the wave
function interpretation, since information is leaking into
our world from alternate worlds, but it does not disprove
that interpretation.  It just creates a situation where the
collapse model strains credulity even more than it usually
does.

